    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2971" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ăpelles</span></b> , is
		(voc. Apella, <i><span class="en">Plaut. Poen. 5, 4, 101</span></i>, as if from the
		Doric <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀπελλᾶς</span>), m., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀπελλῆς</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a distinguished Greek painter in the
				time of Alexander the Great</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 35,
				10, 36, § 10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Brut.
				18, 70</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Off. 3, 2, 10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Fam. 1,
			9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Prop. 4, 8, 11 al.</span></i>—Hence,
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ăpellēus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Apelles</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">opus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					7, 83</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tabulae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop. 1, 2, 22 al.</span></i>
			</div>
